{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472588-perfection-of-form-and-weapons","id":472588,"title":"Perfection of Form and Weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T05:57:06-07:00","id":472588,"title":"Perfection of Form and Weapons","content":"Does the damage bonus of weapons count as an equipment bonus for this Gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:12:07-07:00","id":472612,"title":"","content":"I would probably say 'no', since the Facet is meant to improve a tool, not a weapon (yes, weapons are 'tools', but the distinction here is clear, I thnik). That said, you can do whatever you want. I'd suggest making it +1 for every 2 or 3 successes instead, though, since the intent of the Facet is to give dice, not successes, while a weapon's damage bonus does the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:04:03-07:00","id":472766,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with the no. The way the rules are written Damage in 2e isn't an equipment bonus (it doesn't add dice to your roll). Weapons can count as equipment as well, and Perfection of Form should boost them appropriately in that context.<br /> <br /> Gebbethine's suggestion works well though, but I'd go with 3 successes on a math level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T17:31:39-07:00","id":473534,"title":"","content":"Page 168:<br /> &quot;A weapon\u2019s damage rating adds bonus successes to a successful attack roll. When a weapon might help out in other ways \u2014 using a chain to grapple someone, or a gun to intimidate them, add the weapon\u2019s damage rating as an equipment modifier.&quot;<br /> <br /> So you can use it on a weapon, it just doesn't modify the damage rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:21:42-07:00","id":473581,"title":"","content":"Sweet, thanks for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}